<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">African diaspora</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The African diaspora refers to the communities of people of African descent living outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, largely created by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a>. Enslaved people from regions such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kongo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo</a> empires carried languages, religious practices and cultural traditions to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a> and Kongo influences remain visible in religions and cultures in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> and elsewhere.</p></div>
